course: dictionary
lesson: 5147
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Iris is one of them. You cannot tell which meaning is right from the word alone, so look at the words around it. «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint: the black dot in your eye, the pupil, shrinks fast, because the coloured ring around it, the iris, is a muscle that lets in less light.» Here, the clues are eye, pupil and light, so iris means the coloured ring in your eye.
explain: Now try a different sentence: «Mum planted blue irises along the fence.» Planted is a clue. You plant seeds and flowers in a garden, so irises here are tall garden flowers. A girl called Iris would be a name, and it would start with a capital letter. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence in place of the word. If «the coloured ring in your eye was planted along the fence» makes no sense, you have picked the wrong meaning. If the sentence still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: The iris is the coloured ring around the pupil in your eye.
fact: The iris gets bigger or smaller to control how much light goes into the eye.
fact: An iris is a tall garden flower with sword-shaped leaves; its flowers are often purple, blue, yellow or white.
fact: Iris is also a girl's name, and in Greek myths Iris was the goddess of the rainbow.
fact: A word with several meanings can be understood by checking the clues in the sentence around it.
exercise: «The pupil is a hole that lets light into the eye; the coloured iris around it is a muscle.» What does iris mean here? | A girl's name | A tall garden flower with sword-shaped leaves | *The coloured ring around the pupil | A rainbow in the sky
exercise: «Mum planted blue irises along the fence.» What does irises mean here? | *Tall garden flowers | Dark, shady corners of a garden | Goddesses of the rainbow | The coloured rings in people's eyes
exercise: «Iris is coming to my party on Saturday.» What is Iris here? | A garden flower | *A girl's name | A goddess who lives in the sky, like a bird | The coloured ring in an eye
test: «In bright sunlight, your iris makes your pupil smaller.» What does the iris control? | Which way you look | *How much light gets into the eye | How loud sounds are | How tall you grow
test: In Greek myths, Iris was the goddess of what? | The moon | The harvest | The sea | *The rainbow
exam: What does the iris do in bright light? | *It makes the pupil smaller, so less light gets in | It makes the eye close completely | It makes the pupil bigger, so more light gets in | It changes the shape of the flower
